fy all fentanyl-related substances as Schedule I controlled substances, meaning they would be treated as having high abuse potential and no accepted medical use. It sets the same criminal penalties and quantity thresholds for fentanyl-related substances as currently apply to fentanyl analogues. The bill also creates a streamlined registration process for researchers studying Schedule I substances and makes it easier for registered researchers to conduct certain activities without additional permits.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"People caught up in the criminal law, and victims of crime.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"H001086","score":0.08496351694573398},"overlapCount":58},"meaning":{"percentile":40.085186938002835,"median":0.01073720309570498,"n":6339,"ordinary":[],"unattributedShare":0.8165537008107441}},{"billId":"119-hr-29","bioguideId":"M001239","cycle":2026,"score":0.008168801094252779,"matches":[{"industry":"legal","donorAmount":11541.98,"donorShare":0.012909892452087767,"billConfidence":0.85,"contribution":0.006270519191014058},{"industry":"government","donorAmount":3300,"donorShare":0.003691103700741955,"billConfidence":0.9,"contribution":0.00189828190323872}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":2026,"billClassificationMethod":"llm","unclassifiedDonorShare":0.8165537008107441},"bill":{"id":"119-hr-29","congress":119,"billType":"hr","billNumber":"29","title":"Laken Riley Act","introducedDate":"2025-01-03","latestActionDate":"2025-02-10","latestActionText":"Read the second time. Placed on Senate Legislative Calendar under General Orders. Calendar No. 10.","policyArea":"Immigration","subjects":["Border security and unlawful immigration","Civil actions and liability","Crimes against property","Criminal inve